$ fake_git --help
usage: fake_git [--authors] [--help] [--markdown] [--version] {init,commit,tag} ...

A toy git-like program demonstrating FLAP

Optional switches:
  --authors, -a
      default value .false.
      Print the authors
  --help, -h
      Print this help message
  --markdown, -md
      Save this help message in a Markdown file
  --version, -v
      Print version

Commands:
  init
      Initialise versioning
  commit
      Commit changes to the current branch
  tag
      Tag the current commit

For more detailed commands help try:
  fake_git init -h,--help
  fake_git commit -h,--help
  fake_git tag -h,--help

Examples:
  fake_git --help
  fake_git init
  fake_git commit -m "fix bug #1"
  fake_git tag -a "v2.1.5"
